body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If `cloneJson` is called with `undefined` (which can happen if optional properties are missing in malformed input files), `JSON.stringify(undefined)` returns `undefined`, and `JSON.parse(undefined)` will throw a `SyntaxError` and crash the script. We should defensively guard against `undefined` to ensure the validator fails closed gracefully instead of crashing.

```suggestion
function cloneJson(value) {
  if (value === undefined) return undefined;
  return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value));
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Ensure validators fail closed gracefully for null, malformed, or non-record inputs, validate manifest array fields and expected source artifact roles, and verify that upstream source files exist and parse as valid JSON.
</details>

