If `pageAssets` contains any null or non-record elements, mapping over them to access `ms_page_asset_id` will throw a `TypeError`. We should filter out non-record elements using `isRecord` to ensure robust, fail-closed execution.

```javascript
function indexPageAssets(pageAssets) {
  return Object.fromEntries(
    pageAssets
      .filter(isRecord)
      .map((pageAsset) => [pageAsset.ms_page_asset_id, pageAsset])
  );
}
```

